Subject: [PATCH 085/119] docs: the display chain, the camera grade, and how to
 make a look

- README: the S4/S5 section replaces the "expect it to look off until S4" warning with the chain
  as it now runs, and the note that the stock LDR sliders go inert by design. Four property
  tables: White Balance (Tint added, and what "neutral" means on each path), Grade, Look, Output.
  Every default is documented as the exact identity it is.
- ConsoleReference: the twelve new post-effect bus params - the two LUT slots with their grid
  sizes, and the grade block - with what a size of 0 means in each slot.
- SceneReferredSpec: status lines for S4 and S5, with the three deviations stated (per-pixel
  chain instead of the combined LUT, the LUT helper kept out of the shared shader header, 65^3
  shipped as the default) and the two follow-ups (.cdl interchange, the D12 EXR round-trip which
  waits on S6).
- docs/SceneReferredLook.md, new: the chain in one diagram, where to install the shipped ODTs and
  how the path is resolved, how to bake another, how to author an LMT in Resolve on an ACEScct
  timeline, the identity-cube test that proves the whole loader in one look, what the parser
  refuses and why, when to grade on the camera instead, and a symptom table.

